DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       llllvvmm--ssiizzee  is a tool that prints size information for binary files.  It
       is intended to be a drop-in replacement for GNU's ssiizzee.

       The tool prints size information for each iinnppuutt specified. If no  input
       is  specified, the program prints size information for aa..oouutt. If "--" is
       specified as an input file, llllvvmm--ssiizzee reads a file  from  the  standard
       input  stream. If an input is an archive, size information will be dis‐
       played for all its members.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --AA     Equivalent to _-_-_f_o_r_m_a_t with a value of ssyyssvv.

       ----aarrcchh==<<aarrcchh>>
              Architecture(s) from Mach-O universal binaries to display infor‐
              mation for.

       --BB     Equivalent to _-_-_f_o_r_m_a_t with a value of bbeerrkkeelleeyy.

       ----ccoommmmoonn
              Include  ELF common symbol sizes in bss size for bbeerrkkeelleeyy output
              format, or as a separate section entry for ssyyssvv output.  If  not
              specified, these symbols are ignored.

       --dd     Equivalent to _-_-_r_a_d_i_x with a value of 1100.

       --ll     Display  verbose address and offset information for segments and
              sections in Mach-O files in ddaarrwwiinn format.

       ----ffoorrmmaatt==<<ffoorrmmaatt>>
              Set the output format to the <<ffoorrmmaatt>> specified. Available <<ffoorr‐‐
              mmaatt>> options are bbeerrkkeelleeyy (the default), ssyyssvv and ddaarrwwiinn.

              Berkeley  output  summarises  text,  data  and bss sizes in each
              file, as shown below for a typical pair of ELF files:

                 $ llvm-size --format=berkeley test.o test2.o
                    text    data     bss     dec     hex filename
                     182      16       5     203      cb test.elf
                      82       8       1      91      5b test2.o

              For Mach-O files, the output format is slightly different:

                 $ llvm-size --format=berkeley macho.obj macho2.obj
                 __TEXT  __DATA  __OBJC  others  dec     hex
                 4       8       0       0       12      c       macho.obj
                 16      32      0       0       48      30      macho2.obj

              Sysv output displays size and address information for most  sec‐
              tions, with each file being listed separately:

                 $ llvm-size --format=sysv test.elf test2.o
                    test.elf  :
                    section       size      addr
                    .eh_frame       92   2097496
                    .text           90   2101248
                    .data           16   2105344
                    .bss             5   2105360
                    .comment       209         0
                    Total          412

                    test2.o  :
                    section             size   addr
                    .text                 26      0
                    .data                  8      0
                    .bss                   1      0
                    .comment             106      0
                    .note.GNU-stack        0      0
                    .eh_frame             56      0
                    .llvm_addrsig          2      0
                    Total                199

              ddaarrwwiinn  format only affects Mach-O input files. If an input of a
              different file format is  specified,  llllvvmm--ssiizzee  falls  back  to
              bbeerrkkeelleeyy format. When producing ddaarrwwiinn format, the tool displays
              information about segments and sections:

                 $ llvm-size --format=darwin macho.obj macho2.obj
                    macho.obj:
                    Segment : 12
                            Section (__TEXT, __text): 4
                            Section (__DATA, __data): 8
                            total 12
                    total 12
                    macho2.obj:
                    Segment : 48
                            Section (__TEXT, __text): 16
                            Section (__DATA, __data): 32
                            total 48
                    total 48

       ----hheellpp,, --hh
              Display a summary of command line options.

       --mm     Equivalent to _-_-_f_o_r_m_a_t with a value of ddaarrwwiinn.

       --oo     Equivalent to _-_-_r_a_d_i_x with a value of 88.

       ----rraaddiixx==<<vvaalluuee>>
              Display size information in the specified radix. Permitted  val‐
              ues  are 88, 1100 (the default) and 1166 for octal, decimal and hexa‐
              decimal output respectively.

              Example:

                 $ llvm-size --radix=8 test.o
                    text    data     bss     oct     hex filename
                    0152      04      04     162      72 test.o

                 $ llvm-size --radix=10 test.o
                    text    data     bss     dec     hex filename
                     106       4       4     114      72 test.o

                 $ llvm-size --radix=16 test.o
                    text    data     bss     dec     hex filename
                    0x6a     0x4     0x4     114      72 test.o

       ----ttoottaallss,, --tt
              Applies only to bbeerrkkeelleeyy output format. Display the  totals  for
              all listed fields, in addition to the individual file listings.

              Example:

                 $ llvm-size --totals test.elf test2.o
                    text    data     bss     dec     hex filename
                     182      16       5     203      cb test.elf
                      82       8       1      91      5b test2.o
                     264      24       6     294     126 (TOTALS)

